{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd","id":853150,"title":"Totems: 1st ed vs CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-25T13:42:02-07:00","id":853150,"title":"Totems: 1st ed vs CofD","content":"Which totems are better and why, what do you think? In 1st edition, totems could buff character way stronger, but this required a lot of xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:01:49-07:00","id":853156,"title":"","content":"I like the 2e version much better. Partially because I like the 2e rules for spirits in general better, and partly because the rules for Totem creation are much more streamlined. Also, since you don't have to split points between making the Totem stronger and increasing its bonuses, you don't end up with super powerful Totems that grant incredibly weak bonuses or incredibly weak Totems that grant super powerful bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:15:23-07:00","id":853159,"title":"","content":"I agree with Charlaquin, adding that totems seem to be a more important member of the pack, and the rites second edition has to empower them and its participation on the hunt can really help keep it from <i>seeming</i> like a fancy version of the Mentor merit.<br /> <br /> I really dig's Stew's idea that a player could play the totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:24:03-07:00","id":853162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853156#post853156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since you don't have to split points between making the Totem stronger and increasing its bonuses, you don't end up with super powerful Totems that grant incredibly weak bonuses or incredibly weak Totems that grant super powerful bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, but it's mostly because they don't give bonuses anymore. Only +1 to some trait, that's it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:28:05-07:00","id":853163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853162#post853162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, but it's mostly because they don't give bonuses anymore. Only +1 to some trait, that's it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or granting a Merit dot that the characters don't have to have the prerequisites for, or can make your traits exceed the normal limit of 5 (or higher)?<br /> <br /> Methinks you're underestimating the power of 2e totems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:42:19-07:00","id":853169,"title":"","content":"It's true, but in first edition you could obtain a lot of dots to any trait. It was expensive, of cause, but at least you have an opportunity/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:45:17-07:00","id":853171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853162#post853162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, but it's mostly because they don't give bonuses anymore. Only +1 to some trait, that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They grant a set exp amount worth of benefits to everyone in the pack. The players decide as a group what to spend that experience on, so it can easily be Skills, Specialties, Merits, Attributes, Primal Urge, Rites, or anything else you can think of to spend exp on. And it grants that benefit to the whole pack, including peripheral human and Wolf-Blooded members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:47:43-07:00","id":853173,"title":"","content":"You aren't limited to raising things by a single dot. With a basic totem out of character generation, provided you've placed an emphasis on your totem by having your wolf-blooded packmates have the totem merit, you can get +1 Skill and 1 Merit or Skill Specialty. Just a little bit more and you can have two Skill dots and a Merit or Specialty, or an Attribute and a Merit or Specialty. If you went all out or have a particularly large pack you can have up to +5 in a single Skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:26:38-07:00","id":853189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853171#post853171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They grant a set exp amount worth of benefits to everyone in the pack. The players decide as a group what to spend that experience on, so it can easily be Skills, Specialties, Merits, Attributes, Primal Urge, Rites, or anything else you can think of to spend exp on. And it grants that benefit to the whole pack, including peripheral human and Wolf-Blooded members.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in 1st ed it was mostly the same, wasn't it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Just a little bit more and you can have two Skill dots and a Merit or Specialty, or an Attribute and a Merit or Specialty. If you went all out or have a particularly large pack you can have up to +5 in a single Skill. </div> </div> </div> May be, but again iwasn't it worked the same way in 1st edition? Look like totems were nerfed (while every other thing was empowered in 2ed), and I just don't like, when werewolves get nerfed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:46:15-07:00","id":853203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853189#post853189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But in 1st ed it was mostly the same, wasn't it?<br /> May be, but again iwasn't it worked the same way in 1st edition? Look like totems were nerfed (while every other thing was empowered in 2ed), and I just don't like, when werewolves get nerfed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first it was a lot more expensive, costing 30 Experience to raise an Attribute by one, and you couldn't go above normal maximums. In addition the abilities didn't help out wolf-blooded, wolves, humans, vampires, or anything else you had in the pack like it does in second edition. While human packmates can't go above their maximum, if it reaches their maximum they gain 8-again on all rolls involving the trait.<br /> <br /> In addition, you had to purchase Totem merits to build up the totem and gain pack benefits separately. While in second edition the Totem merit adds to both simultaneously.<br /> <br /> It's really not a nerf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-25-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:57:31-07:00","id":853209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853189#post853189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in 1st ed it was mostly the same, wasn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the fact that you had to choose between better bonuses and making the Totem spirit itself stronger. In 2e, you get both at the same time, albeit at a fixed rate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853189#post853189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May be, but again iwasn't it worked the same way in 1st edition? Look like totems were nerfed (while every other thing was empowered in 2ed), and I just don't like, when werewolves get nerfed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totems were <i>streamlined</i>. Don't mistake streamlining for nerfing. Sure, you can no longer dump all of your Totem dots into giving you increased attributes or whatever. But the trade off is, you don't have to spend exorbitant amounts of experience to make both your Totem itself and the bonuses it grants any good, you don't have to choose between making your Totem stronger and getting better bonuses from it, the bonuses affect everyone in the pack, including human and Wolf-Blooded members, the bonuses can bring werewolf members above their Attribute/stat cap, and the process is simpler and more consistent. That's a net buff in my book, and a big one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-25-2016, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T21:57:54-07:00","id":853332,"title":"","content":"Another buff to Totem in 2e?<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded pack members can contribute a Totem dot. So a pack with a small number of werewolves, and large support network of wolf-blooded can have a far more powerful Totem than they could in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:37:42-07:00","id":853464,"title":"","content":"The honest only real loss from 1e totems is that 2e totems cant grant gifts. I always thought that was cool, a totem granting gifts, and I would maybe even houserule that sometime, though it might complicate things. If you already have the facet maybe your renown for it counts as one higher? I dont know. This is for another time.<br /> <br /> Things that are gone thankfully are once per story bonuses, and pack pool bonuses. I much prefer the static consistent bonus of being connected to a totem. Also totemic empowerment is my favourite rite hands down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:55:15-07:00","id":853571,"title":"","content":"You can capture some of the aspects of granting Gifts by having the Totem grant supernatural Merits (even ones that werewolves might not be able to buy). This can still have the feel of the Totem granting supernatural powers, but slots into the system without the issues 2e Gifts would. It also allows non-werewolf members of the pack to benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:01:28-07:00","id":853574,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of giving Rites as Totem benefits. Heh. &quot;Only taught to Storm Lords&quot; my ass!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:12:16-07:00","id":853700,"title":"","content":"Can you really get Primal Urge from a totem? I thought they couldn't do that for the same reason they can't grant facets. There's no equivalent for the non-werewolf pack members to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:30:24-07:00","id":853709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=853700#post853700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you really get Primal Urge from a totem? I thought they couldn't do that for the same reason they can't grant facets. There's no equivalent for the non-werewolf pack members to get.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Strictly</i> speaking, no. The Totem Creation rules say &quot; The players buy a benefit \u2014 an Attribute, Skill, Skill Specialty, or Merit \u2014 with a pool of Experiences, with the number of Experiences based on the number of Totem points.&quot; I'm a bit more generous with what can be bought with Totem than RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:35:52-07:00","id":853710,"title":"","content":"The only issue I can see with Primal Urge from Totem is that PU can't go over 10, and there's no simple solution to what you'd replace it with if you ever get that far in your game. Cost-wise, it's expensive enough that it shouldn't really be overpowering.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:15:32-07:00","id":854012,"title":"","content":"Couldn't a Totem, as a spirit, be a really convenient source to learn Gifts from naturally though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:42:30-07:00","id":854020,"title":"","content":"Yeah. They'd need to be resonant with it, but that seems like the obvious place to start if you want one. The way talens work now they could supply the power for those too, at least sparingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:07:03-07:00","id":854038,"title":"","content":"Yes, totems are a very accessible source for whatever Gifts are appropriate for them. Of course, a totem may still have standards it wants met before it will teach a particular Gift, or have trials it sets pack members so they have to prove themselves, or demand particular offerings and gathra. Still, having a well-inclined totem <i>right there </i>makes the whole process convenient and means that packs will likely tend to have lots of members with the Gifts that their totem can give.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T13:59:54-07:00","id":854196,"title":"","content":"Possibly stretching spoiler remit here, and I hate contradicting Acrozatarim, but unless Stew has made a last minute change to <i>The Pack</i>, a totem explicitly <b>can't</b> impart Gifts on its pack. (For reasons I can discuss more when the book is released.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:08:02-07:00","id":854201,"title":"","content":"Oh snap. It's going down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:10:04-07:00","id":854204,"title":"","content":"By reasons do you mean reasons you decided to make it not possible or reasons they can't do it in-game? Because I'm kinda drawing a blank as to how being bonded to a pack could interfere with carving occult scars into their flesh/spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:10:33-07:00","id":854205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=854196#post854196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly stretching spoiler remit here, and I hate contradicting Acrozatarim, but unless Stew has made a last minute change to <i>The Pack</i>, a totem explicitly <b>can't</b> impart Gifts on its pack. (For reasons I can discuss more when the book is released.)</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bReally? I must have missed that bit when I read through the drafts - sorry!<br /> <br /> Well, until The Pack comes out, I'm still right! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:10:57-07:00","id":854206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=854204#post854204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By reasons do you mean reasons you decided to make it not possible or reasons they can't do it in-game? Because I'm kinda drawing a blank as to how being bonded to a pack could interfere with carving occult scars into their flesh/spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>In-universe reasons. (Edit: To be clear - reasons that exist day-to-day for the people who live in the CoD, not out-of-character reasons.)<br /> <br /> (Want to say more. Shouldn't.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=854205#post854205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bReally? I must have missed that bit when I read through the drafts - sorry!<br /> <br /> Well, until The Pack comes out, I'm still right! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&lt; Futurama &gt; You are technically correct. The best kind of correct. &lt; / Futurama &gt;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-27-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:57:16-07:00","id":854220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=854196#post854196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly stretching spoiler remit here, and I hate contradicting Acrozatarim, but unless Stew has made a last minute change to <i>The Pack</i>, a totem explicitly <b>can't</b> impart Gifts on its pack. (For reasons I can discuss more when the book is released.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Totems <i>will</i> be nerfed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T15:11:47-07:00","id":854225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=854220#post854220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Totems <i>will</i> be nerfed?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you believe they're nerfed because they can't offer Gifts, then yes. Gifts, however, are far less expensive and for the amount of experience you would pay to get enough Totem merits to get one to give you a gift, you could buy everyone in the pack several Gifts.<br /> <br /> You seem to have moved from asking which one people prefer to trying to label something as nerfed or not, are you no longer interested in peoples opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T15:31:11-07:00","id":854228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/853150-totems-1st-ed-vs-cofd?p=854220#post854220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Totems <i>will</i> be nerfed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. In 1E when you wanted a Gift you found a spirit to ask, performed whatever task and trials it wanted from you - and it always required something, because spirits can't give anything away for free, ever - then paid XP to get Gift. This spirit could be the totem, but the only benefit to that was that you knew where to find it, but honestly this is a tiny benefit, because if you can't find a spirit, you're not trying. In 2E the process is the same, except the spirit can't be your pack's totem.<br /> <br /> Objectively, 2E totems are better than 1E. What they give up in some areas, they gain in many others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T15:37:27-07:00","id":854232,"title":"","content":"The first totem dot is free. So if a five-person campaign goes for the standard five werewolf, five wolfblooded, five to ten human pack the book suggests that's 10 totem points you can get without spending a dot of your character's merit allotment. That's a three-experience bonus for absolutely nothing, and the entire pack gets access to it. If everyone spends just one merit dot on totem after that it gets bumped up to five, for a net profit of four. For just two dots each (plus another wolfblood, why not?) you're looking at 10 experiences to play with. <br /> <br /> A totem is basically just a load of free shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:08:33-07:00","id":861239,"title":"","content":"OK, totems become more flexible. I get it. Now I just want to ask about Totem points/Experience. In book, it was described as:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Totem Points Advantage</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1-8 One Experiences</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">9-14 Three Experiences</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">15-20 Five Experiences</span></span><br /> <b>20+</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Ten Experiences</span></span> </div> </div> </div>This &quot;20+&quot; always give 10? What if the pack accumulate 30-40-50 Totem Points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","ra